Z||000000||FieroLisa||11-22-2001||01:32 PM||||Jonathan (SlammedFiero) made me a short shifter, but my problem is, the neck of it is too thick to work with a stock shift boot. So does anyone know how I can get a shift boot made that will fit by having a wider opening? Or should I keep it ghetto with the electrical tape rigging its got now??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (To go with my $5.99 pepboys seat covers, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
