Z||000004||jimmybpei||11-22-2001||06:13 PM||||Lisa,<P>First of all did you just cut down the stock shifter, and now there is a lot of boot binding up the shifer. <P>If the answer is yes just take the boo to an upolstry shop and have the boot cut down to fit(the part of the boot closest to the knob)<P>Hope this is the help your looking for, this is what i did to my 5 speed caddy and my v6 auto, they both work fine.<P>Later<BR>Jimmy B.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Reality||11-22-2001||06:32 PM||||The boot would have to fit a rod about 1 1/4 in diameter<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||11-22-2001||11:52 PM||||one of the cars i got had that done. i haven't driven it but just rowing it through the gears it feels like the boot is bunching up and keeping it from going into 2nd and 4th well (4 speed) i'm thinking about a gated plate.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||11-23-2001||12:25 AM||||Lisa, when you come down to Raleigh in Dec., I can show you what I did with my boot when I shortened my shifter.  I'm still using the stock boot, and no permanent changes were made so I can revert back to stock if I want.  Looks pretty good, I think.  I am using a shortened factory shifter, though.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sage||11-23-2001||12:28 AM||||Don't want to speak for him, but you might try My7Fieros.  He posted pics of some he made a while back. They looked great!<P>He may be able to do a custom one for you.<P>Another thought, if I understand your problem correctly, is if the boot top opening is not wide enough, maybe you can take out the stitching and redo it to the width you need or add some elastic or other material. You could also shorten the neck if it needs it this way.  Just some thoughts.<P>Hope you get it taken care of.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
